kunzite: the AMFI stand-in marks the code it accepts CS_ENTITLEMENTS_VALIDATED, as AMFI does for code
whose entitlements it trusts; exec copies the flag from the blob to the process (kern_exec.c). On #58
every process's status was 0x26000001 (VALID, PLATFORM_BINARY, SIGNED) and tccd granted nothing by
com.apple.private.tcc.allow: assetsd, whose signature carries kTCCServicePhotos and whose
entitlements csops and csops_audittoken return in full (XML and DER), was denied Photos and threw
"assetsd requires TCCPhotosService access" (no Photos, no wallpapers, no screenshots); a test
program signed with the same entitlement was denied too. tccd keeps each client's codesignStatus.
[guess, to test on the next boot: that is tccd's gate.]

diff --git a/bsd/kern/sweet_amfi.c b/bsd/kern/sweet_amfi.c
index 49ead96..98eb498 100644
--- a/bsd/kern/sweet_amfi.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/sweet_amfi.c
@@ -271,6 +271,11 @@ STARTUP(EARLY_BOOT, STARTUP_RANK_MIDDLE, sweet_amfi_register);
  * processes without it. Every signed binary on the root filesystem is a
  * platform binary. New signatures (ubc_cs_blob_add passes its writable copy;
  * revalidation passes the read-only blob itself) get their entitlements here.
+ * And CS_ENTITLEMENTS_VALIDATED, which AMFI sets on code whose entitlements it
+ * trusts: exec copies it to the process too. Without it (kunzite #58: status
+ * 0x26000001 everywhere) tccd granted nothing by com.apple.private.tcc.allow:
+ * assetsd, whose signature has kTCCServicePhotos, was denied Photos and threw
+ * "assetsd requires TCCPhotosService access". [guess, to test: tccd's check.]
  */
 static int
 sweet_amfi_vnode_check_signature(struct vnode *vp, __unused struct label *label,
@@ -280,7 +285,7 @@ sweet_amfi_vnode_check_signature(struct vnode *vp, __unused struct label *label,
     __unused char **fatal_failure_desc, __unused size_t *fatal_failure_desc_len)
 {
 	mount_t mp = vnode_mount(vp);
-	*cs_flags |= CS_SIGNED;
+	*cs_flags |= CS_SIGNED | CS_ENTITLEMENTS_VALIDATED;
 	if (mp != NULL && (vfs_flags(mp) & MNT_ROOTFS)) {
 		*cs_flags |= CS_PLATFORM_BINARY;
 	}
